{
  "title": "38: Saad ص",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nصٓ‌ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ ذِى الذِّكْرِؕ‏(1)\nSAA WAL QURAANIL ZIL AZ-ZEKRE.\nSad, (S) By the Qur’an (which) is full of admonition\nبَلِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِىْ عِزَّةٍ وَّشِقَاقٍ‏(2)\nBALIL LAZEENA KAFAROO FEE E’EZZATIN WWASHEQAAQIN.\nNay! those who disbelieve are (steeped) in self-exaltation and opposition.\nكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ فَنَادَوْا وَّلَاتَ حِيْنَ مَنَاصٍ‏(3)\nKAM AHLAKNAL MIN QABLEHIM MIN QARNIN FANAADAWA WWALAATA HEENA MANAASIN.\nHow many We did destroy of the generations before them, and they cried while (there was no longer) the time to escape.\nوَعَجِبُوْۤا اَنْ جَآءَهُمْ مُّنْذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ‌ وَقَالَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا سٰحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(4)\nWAA’AJEBOOA AN JAAA-AHUM MMUNZERUN MINHUM WA QAALA KAAFEROON HAAZAA SAAHERUN KAZZAABUN.\nAnd they did wonder that came unto them a warner from among themselves, and said the disbelievers: “This is a sorcerer, a great liar.\nاَجَعَلَ الْاٰلِهَةَ اِلٰهًا وَّاحِدًاۖۚ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَشَىْءٌ عُجَابٌ‏(5)\nAAJAA’ALA AL-AAALEHATA ELAAHANW WAAHEDANW INNAL HAAZAA LASHAAUN U’UJAABUN.\nWhat! maketh he the gods to be but one God? Verily this is a thing indeed strange!\nوَانْطَلَقَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْهُمْ اَنِ امْشُوْا وَاصْبِرُوْا عَلٰٓى اٰلِهَتِكُمْ‌ ‌ۖۚ‌ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَشَىْءٌ يُّرَادُ ۖ‌ۚ‏(6)\nWAANTALAQA MALA-O MINHUM SAALEHAN AMSHOOA WAASBEROOA A’LAA AAALEHATEKUM INNAL HAAZAA LASHAAUN YYURAADU.\nAnd the chiefs from them get away (impatiently, exhorting the others saying): “Walk ye away hence and be steadfast unto your gods: verily this is (but) with something designed against us!\nمَا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِى الْمِلَّةِ الْاٰخِرَةِ ۖۚ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا اخْتِلَاقٌ ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(7)\nMAA SAMEA’NAA BEHAAZAA FIL AL-MELLATE AAKHERATE IN HAAZAA ILLAA AKHTELAAQUN.\nWe heard not of this in the former creed. This is nothing but an imposture:\nءَاُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِنَا‌ؕ بَلْ هُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْ ذِكْرِىْ‌ۚ بَلْ لَّمَّا يَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِؕ‏(8)\nAANZELA A’LAYHE AZ-ZEKRU MIN BAYNENAA BAL HUM FEE SHAKKIM MIN ZEKREAA BAL LAMMAA YAZOOQOOA A’AZAABE.\n(What!) Hath the reminder been sent down (only) unto him among us?” Nay! they are in doubt about My reminder, Nay! they have yet tasted not My chastisement!\nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمْ خَزَآئِنُ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّكَ الْعَزِيْزِ الْوَهَّابِ‌ۚ‏(9)\nAM E’ENDAHUM KHAZAAENUS RAHMATE RABBEKA A’ZEEZIL AL-WAHHAABE.\nOr is it that with them are the treasures of the mercy of thy Lord, the All-Mighty, the Greater Bestower?\nاَمْ لَهُمْ مُّلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا‌فَلْيَرْتَقُوْا فِى الْاَسْبَابِ‏(10)\nAM LAHUM MMULKU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHUMAAFALYARTAQOOA FIL AL-AASBAABE.\nOr is it that unto them belongeth the kingdom of the heavens and the earth and what is between them? Then let them ascend with means\nجُنْدٌ مَّا هُنَالِكَ مَهْزُوْمٌ مِّنَ الْاَحْزَابِ‏(11)\nJUNDUM MAA HONAALEKAB MAHZOOMUN MENAL AL-AAHZAABE.\nAnd what a mighty host of the clans shall here be routed.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٌ وَّفِرْعَوْنُ ذُو الْاَوْتَادِۙ‏(12)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WWAA’AADUN WWAFERA’AWNU ZUL AWTAADIL.\nAnd did belie before them the people of Noah, and ’Ad, and Pharaoh the lord, of stakes (of established authority),\nوَثَمُوْدُ وَقَوْمُ لُوْطٍ وَّاَصْحٰبُ لْئَیْكَةِ‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الْاَحْزَابُ‏(13)\nWA SAMOODO WA QAWMO LOOTIM WWAASHAABU LAKATE OOLAAA-EKA YAATIL.\nAnd Thamood and the people of Lot and the dwellers of the wood; these were the clans.\nاِنْ كُلٌّ اِلَّا كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ عِقَابِ‏(14)\nIN KULLUL ILLAA KAZZABA AR-RUSULA FA HAQQA E’EQAABE.\nNot one (of them) but did belie the apostles (from Me) so just was (My) retribution.\nوَمَا يَنْظُرُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً مَّا لَهَا مِنْ فَوَاقٍ‏(15)\nWA MAA YANZORUL HAAOOLAAA-E ILLAA SAYHATANW WAAHEDATAN MAA LAHAA MIN FAWAAQIN.\nAnd wait not these (infidels) but a single (Trumpet) blast, there shall be no delaying it.\nوَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا عَجِّلْ لَّنَا قِطَّنَا قَبْلَ يَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ‏(16)\nWA QAALOO RABBANAA A’AJJEL LANAA QETTANAA QABLA YAWMIL HESAAB.\nAnd (yet) they (dare to) say: “O’ Our Lord! hasten on unto us our lot before the Day of Reckoning\nاِصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَا دَاوٗدَ ذَا الْاَيْدِ‌ۚ اِنَّهٗۤ اَوَّابٌ‏(17)\nAESBER A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WAAZKUR A’ABDANAA DAAWOODA ZAL AL-AAYDE INNAHU AAWABUN.\nBear (thou) with patience what they say, and remember Our servant David, (who was blessed by Us) with the strength of hand, (and yet) verily he (was the one who) Oft-turned (unto Us in patience).\nاِنَّا سَخَّرْنَا الْجِبَالَ مَعَهٗ يُسَبِّحْنَ بِالْعَشِىِّ وَالْاِشْرَاقِۙ‏(18)\nINNAA SAKKHARNAA JEBAALA MA-A’HU YUSABBEHNA BIL-A’ASHEAAAE WAL AESHRAAQE.\nVerily, We did subject the mountains to join with him in the hymns (of their Lord) at the night-fall and at sunrise,\nوَالطَّيْرَ مَحْشُوْرَةً ؕ كُلٌّ لَّهٗۤ اَوَّابٌ‏(19)\nWA TAYRA MAHSHOORATAN KULLUL LAHU AAWABUN.\nAnd the birds assembled together (to sing the hymns unto their Lord) and were unto him obedient.\nوَشَدَدْنَا مُلْكَهٗ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ الْحِكْمَةَ وَفَصْلَ الْخِطَابِ‏(20)\nWA SHADADNAA MULKAHU WA AATAYNAAHO HIKMATA WAFASLA AL-KHETAABE.\nAnd made We strong his kingdom and bestowed We on him wisdom, and the clear (power of) judgment.\nوَهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ نَبَؤُا الْخَصْمِ‌ۘ اِذْ تَسَوَّرُوا الْمِحْرَابَۙ‏(21)\nWA HAL ATAAKA NABAUA AL-KHASME IZ TASAWROOA AL-MEHRAABA.\nAnd hath the story of the litigants come unto thee? when they climbed the wall into the prayer room?\nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلٰى دَاوٗدَ فَفَزِعَ مِنْهُمْ‌ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ‌ۚ خَصْمٰنِ بَغٰى بَعْضُنَا عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَنَا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا تُشْطِطْ وَاهْدِنَاۤ اِلٰى سَوَآءِ الصِّرَاطِ‏(22)\nIZ DAKHALOO A’LAA DAAWOODA FA-FAZE-A’ MINHUM QAALOO LAA TAKHAF KHASMAANE BAGHAA BAA’ZUNAA A’LAA ELAA FAAHKUM BAYNANAA BIL-HAQQE WA LAA TUSHTET WAAHDENAA ELAA SAWAAA-IL AS-SERAATE.\nWhen entered they upon David and he was frightened of them, said they: “Fear (thou) not, (we are) two litigants, one of us hath exceeded against the other, so decide thou between us with justice, and act not unjustly, and guide us unto the right way.\nاِنَّ هٰذَاۤ اَخِىْ لَهٗ تِسْعٌ وَّتِسْعُوْنَ نَعْجَةً وَّلِىَ نَعْجَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ فَقَالَ اَكْفِلْنِيْهَا وَعَزَّنِىْ فِى الْخِطَابِ‏(23)\nINNAL HAAZAA AAKHEAA LAHU TESA’UN WWATESU’OONA NAA’JATAN WWALEAAA NAA’JATUN WWAAHEDATUN FAQAALA AAKFELNEEHAA WAA’AZZANEAA FIL AL-KHETAABE.\nVerily, this my brother; he hath ninety and nine ewes and for me is but a single ewe;” but said he, “Make me the owner of that (also), and hath prevailed over me in arguing\nقَالَ لَقَدْ ظَلَمَكَ بِسُؤَالِ نَعْجَتِكَ اِلٰى نِعَاجِهٖ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الْخُلَطَآءِ لَيَبْغِىْ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَقَلِيْلٌ مَّا هُمْ‌ ؕ وَظَنَّ دَاوٗدُ اَنَّمَا فَتَنّٰهُ فَاسْتَغْفَرَ رَبَّهٗ وَخَرَّ رَاكِعًا وَّاَنَابَ‏(24)\nQAALA LAQAD ZALAMAKA BESUAALE NAA’JATEKA ELAA NEA’AAJEH WA INNA KASEERAA MENAL AL-KHULATAAE LAYABGHEAA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA ILLAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA QALEELUM MAA HUM WA ZANNAS DAA-OODO ANNAMAA FATANNAAHU FAASTAGHFARA WAL WAKHARRA RAAKEA’AN WWAANAABA.\nSaid (David): “Indeed hath he been unjust unto thee in demanding thine ewe to add her to his own ewes: Verily many of the associates act wrongfully unto one another, save those who believe and do good deeds, and few are they!” And David perceived that We had tried him: so asked he the forgiveness of his Lord, and he fell down bowing and oft-turning himself (unto Us).\nفَغَفَرْنَا لَهٗ ذٰ لِكَ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ لَهٗ عِنْدَنَا لَزُلْفٰى وَحُسْنَ مَاٰبٍ‏(25)\nFAGHAFARNAA LAHU ZAA LEKA WA INNA LAHU E’ENDANAA LAZULFAA WAHUSNA MAABIN.\nSo We forgave him that (lapse), and verily for him with Us is a near approach, and an excellent resort.\nيٰدَاوٗدُ اِنَّا جَعَلْنٰكَ خَلِيْفَةً فِى الْاَرْضِ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعِ الْهَوٰى فَيُضِلَّكَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَضِلُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌۢ بِمَا نَسُوْا يَوْمَ الْحِسَابِ‏(26)\nYAA DAA-OODO INNAA JAA’ALNAAKA KHALEEFAH FIL ARZE FAAHKUM BAYNA NAASE BIL-HAQQE WA LAA TATTABEE’E AL-HAWAA FAYUZELLAKA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE INNAL LAZEENA YAZELLOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN BEMAA NASOOA YAWMA HESAAB.\nO’ David! Verily We have appointed thee a vicegerent in the earth, so judge thou between the people with justice and follow not vain desires, lest it should take thee astray from the Way of God; for them shall be a severe chastisement for forgot they the Day of Reckoning.\nوَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمَآءَ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا بَاطِلًا ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ ظَنُّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا‌ۚ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنَ النَّارِؕ‏(27)\nWA MAA KHALAQNAL SAMAAA-AD WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA BAATELAN ZAA LEKA ZANNU LAZEENA KAFAROO LAHUM LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO MENAL NAAR.\nAnd We created not the heavens and the earth in vain: that is the imagination of those who disbelieve; then woe unto those who disbelieve - because of the fire.\nاَمْ نَجْعَلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ كَالْمُفْسِدِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَمْ نَجْعَلُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ كَالْفُجَّارِ‏(28)\nAM NAJA’ALU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE KA-MUFSEDEEN FIL ARZE AM NAJA’ALU MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN KA-FUJJAARE.\n(Or) shall We treat those who believe and do good deeds like the mischief-makers in the earth? Or shall We treat the pious ones like the wicked ones?\nكِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ اِلَيْكَ مُبٰرَكٌ لِّيَدَّبَّرُوْۤا اٰيٰتِهٖ وَلِيَتَذَكَّرَ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(29)\nKETAABUM ANZALNAAHO ELAYKA MUBAARAKUN LLEEDDABBAROOA AAYAATEHI WALEETAZAKKARA ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\n(O’ Our Apostle Muhammad! this Qur’an is) the Book which We have sent down unto thee, abounding in blessings, that they may ponder over its verses, and bear in mind those (who are) endowed with understanding.\nوَوَهَبْنَا لِدَاوٗدَ سُلَيْمٰنَ‌ ؕ نِعْمَ الْعَبْدُ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗۤ اَوَّابٌ ؕ‏(30)\nWA WAHABNAA LE-DAAWOODA SOLAYMAANA NE’MA AL-A’ABDU INNAHU AAWABUN.\nAnd to David We gave (a son) Solomon; an excellent servant (of Ours was he); Verily he was oft-turning (unto Us).\nاِذْ عُرِضَ عَلَيْهِ بِالْعَشِىِّ الصّٰفِنٰتُ الْجِيَادُ ۙ‏(31)\nIZ U’UREZA A’LAYHE BIL-A’ASHEAAAE AS-SAAFENAATU AL-JEEADU.\nRemember when were shown unto him at eventide lightfooted coursers.\nفَقَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اَحْبَبْتُ حُبَّ الْخَيْرِ عَنْ ذِكْرِ رَبِّىْ‌ۚ حَتّٰى تَوَارَتْ بِالْحِجَابِ‏(32)\nFAQAALA INNEE AAHBABTU HUBBA KHAYR A’N ELAA RABBEE HATTAA TAWAARAT BIL-HEJAABE.\nThen said he: “Verily I have loved the good things besides the remembrance of my Lord, until got hidden in the veil (of the darkness of the Night):\nرُدُّوْهَا عَلَىَّؕ فَطَفِقَ مَسْحًۢا بِالسُّوْقِ وَ الْاَعْنَاقِ‏(33)\nRUDDOOHAA A’ALAA FATAFEQA MASHAN BEALSSOOQE WA AL-AAA’NAAQE.\n(Then said he): “Bring it back unto me!” And he began to rub the legs and necks.\nوَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا سُلَيْمٰنَ وَاَلْقَيْنَا عَلٰى كُرْسِيِّهٖ جَسَدًا ثُمَّ اَنَابَ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD FATANNAL SOLAYMAANA WAALQAYNAA A’LAA KURSEEH JASADAN SUMMA AANAABA.\nAnd indeed We did try Solomon, and cast on his throne a (mere) body, then turned he (unto God).\nقَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِىْ وَهَبْ لِىْ مُلْكًا لَّا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لِاَحَدٍ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِىْ‌ۚ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ‏(35)\nQAALA RABBE FIR LEE WAHAB LEE MULKAN LAA LAHAA LE-AHADIN MIN BAA’DEAA INNAKA ANTA AL-WAHHAABU.\nSaid he: “O’ my Lord! Forgive me and grant me a dominion such as shall not befit any one after me, verily Thou alone art the Bounteous Bestower!\nفَسَخَّرْنَا لَهُ الرِّيْحَ تَجْرِىْ بِاَمْرِهٖ رُخَآءً حَيْثُ اَصَابَۙ‏(36)\nFASAKKHARNAA LAHUL AR-REEHA TAJREE LAAHO RUKHAAAN HAYSO ASAABA.\nThen We made subservient unto him the wind: it flew gently at his command whithersoever he desired.\nوَالشَّيٰطِيْنَ كُلَّ بَنَّآءٍ وَّغَوَّاصٍۙ‏(37)\nWA SHAYAATEENA KULLA BANNAAIN WWAGHAWASIN.\nAnd the satans, every builder, and diver,\nوَّاٰخَرِيْنَ مُقَرَّنِيْنَ فِىْ الْاَصْفَادِ‏(38)\nWA AAKHAREENA MUQARRANEENA FEE AL-AASFAADE.\nAnd the others bound in chains;\nهٰذَا عَطَآؤُنَا فَامْنُنْ اَوْ اَمْسِكْ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(39)\nHAAZAA A’ATAAUNAA FAAMNUN AW A’LAYHE BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\nThis is Our gift, now give thou freely or withhold it, (for thou hast) not to render (any) account.\nوَاِنَّ لَهٗ عِنْدَنَا لَزُلْفٰى وَحُسْنَ مَاٰبٍ‏(40)\nWA INNA LAHU E’ENDANAA LAZULFAA WAHUSNA MAABIN.\nAnd verily, for him unto Us is a near approach and an excellent resort.\nوَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَاۤ اَيُّوْبَۘ اِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗۤ اَنِّىْ مَسَّنِىَ الشَّيْطٰنُ بِنُصْبٍ وَّعَذَابٍؕ‏(41)\nWAAZKUR A’ABDANAA AAYWBA IZ NAADAA WAL AANNEAA MASSANEAAA SHAYTAANO BENUSBIN WWAA’AZAABIN.\nAnd remember Our servant Job, when he cried unto his Lord; “Verily, Satan hath caused me an affliction and pain.\nاُرْكُضْ بِرِجْلِكَ‌ ۚ هٰذَا مُغْتَسَلٌ ۢ بَارِدٌ وَّشَرَابٌ‏(42)\nAURKUZ BEREJLEKA HAAZAA MUGHTASALUN BAAREDUN WWASHARAABUN.\n(Said We unto him); “Stamp thou with thy foot” thou this (spring) is (for thee) to wash with, (it is) cool, and a (refreshing) drink\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اَهْلَهٗ وَمِثْلَهُمْ مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنَّا وَذِكْرٰى لِاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(43)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU AHLAHU WAMESLAHUM MMAA’AHUM RAHMATAM MINNAA WAZEKRAA LE-ULIL ULIL ALBAABE.\nAnd gave him his family and the like of them with them, a mercy from Us and a reminder for those with understanding.\nوَخُذْ بِيَدِكَ ضِغْثًا فَاضْرِبْ بِّهٖ وَلَا تَحْنَثْ‌ؕ اِنَّا وَجَدْنٰهُ صَابِرًا‌ ؕ نِعْمَ الْعَبْدُ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗۤ اَوَّابٌ‏(44)\nWAKHUZ BEEDEKA ZEGHSAN FAAZREB BBEH WA LAA TAHNAS INNAA WAJADNAAHU SAABERAN NE’MA AL-A’ABDU INNAHU AAWABUN.\nAnd (it was said unto him) “Take in thine hand a bunch of (thin) stick (like fibre) and strike thou (thy wife) with it, and break not thine oath. Verily We found him steadfast; an excellent servant (was he): Verily he was oft-turning (unto Us).\nوَاذْكُرْ عِبٰدَنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ اُولِى الْاَيْدِىْ وَالْاَبْصَارِ‏(45)\nWAAZKUR E’EBAADANAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA ULIL AL-AAYDEAA WA ULIL ABSAAR.\nAnd remember thou Our servants, Abraham and Isaac and Jacob, men of strength and insight.\nاِنَّاۤ اَخْلَصْنٰهُمْ بِخَالِصَةٍ ذِكْرَى الدَّارِ‌ۚ‏(46)\nINNAA AAKHLASNAAHUM BEKHAALESATIN ZEKRAA AD-DAARE.\nVerily We freed them (from sinning) with a distinction of remembrance of the (eternal) abode.\nوَاِنَّهُمْ عِنْدَنَا لَمِنَ الْمُصْطَفَيْنَ الْاَخْيَارِؕ‏(47)\nWA INNAHUM E’ENDANAA LAMENAS AL-MUSTAFAYNA AL-AAKHYAARE.\nVerily, they are with Us, of the chosen ones, the good ones.\nوَاذْكُرْ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَ الْيَسَعَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ‌ؕ وَكُلٌّ مِّنَ الْاَخْيَارِؕ‏(48)\nWAAZKUR AESMAAE’EELA WA AL-YASAA’A WA ZAL AL-KEFLE KULLUN MENAL AL-AAKHYAARE.\nAnd remember Ishmael and Elisha and Dhu’l-Kifl; they all were of the good ones.\nهٰذَا ذِكْرٌ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ لَحُسْنَ مَاٰبٍۙ‏(49)\nHAAZAA ZEKRUN WA INNA LILMUTTAQEEN LAHUSNA MAABIN.\nThis is a reminder; and verily, for the pious ones there is an excellent resort,\nجَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ مُّفَتَّحَةً لَّهُمُ الْاَبْوَابُ‌ۚ‏(50)\nJANNATIN A’ADNIN MMUFATTAHATAN LAHOMUB AL-AABWAABU.\nGardens of eternal bliss, opened for them are the doors (thereof).\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ فِيْهَا يَدْعُوْنَ فِيْهَا بِفَاكِهَةٍ كَثِيْرَةٍ وَّشَرَابٍ‏(51)\nMUTTAKE-EENA FEEHAA YAD-O’ONA FEEHAA BE-FAAKEHATIN KASEERATIL WWASHARAABIN.\nReclining therein, calling therein for many a fruit and drink.\nوَعِنْدَهُمْ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِ اَتْرَابٌ‏(52)\nWAE’ENDAHUM QAASERAATUT TARFE AATRAABUN.\nAnd with them shall be of modest gaze, equals in age.\nهٰذَا مَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لِيَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ‏(53)\nHAAZAA MAA TOO-A’DOON LE-YAWMIL HESAAB.\nThis is what ye are promised for the Day of Reckoning.\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَرِزْقُنَا مَا لَهٗ مِنْ نَّفَادٍ ‌ۖ ‌ۚ‏(54)\nINNAL HAAZAA LAREZQUNAA MAA LAHU MIN NNAFAADIN.\nVerily, this is Our sustenance; for it there is no end,\nهٰذَا‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ لِلطّٰغِيْنَ لَشَرَّ مَاٰبٍ ۙ‏(55)\nHAAZAA WA INNA LELTTAAGHEENA LASHARRA MAABIN.\nThis (for the righteous); and verily for the wicked ones there a wretched resort,\nجَهَنَّمَ‌ ۚ يَصْلَوْنَهَا‌ ۚ فَبِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ‏(56)\nJAHANNAMA YASLAWNAHAA FA MASALUL MEHAAD.\nHell, they shall enter it, and so evil is the place,\nهٰذَا ۙ فَلْيَذُوْقُوْهُ حَمِيْمٌ وَّغَسَّاقٌ ۙ‏(57)\nHAAZAA FALYAZOOQOOHU HAMEEM WWAGHASSAAQUN.\nEven so, Let them then taste it - boiling water and gore,\nوَّاٰخَرُ مِنْ شَكْلِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجٌ ؕ‏(58)\nWWAAKHARU MIN SHAKLEH AZWAAJUM.\nAnd other (torment) similar to it, of various sort!\nهٰذَا فَوْجٌ مُّقْتَحِمٌ مَّعَكُمْ‌ۚ لَا مَرْحَبًۢا بِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ صَالُوا النَّارِ‏(59)\nHAAZAA FAWJUN MMUQTAHEMUN MMAA’AKUM LAA MARHABAN BEHIM WA INNAHUM SAALOOA NAAR.\n(To their leaders it shall be said) “This army (of your followers) shall be thrown headlong with you! No welcome for them! Verily they shall enter the fire!\nقَالُوْا بَلْ اَنْتُمْ لَا مَرْحَبًۢا بِكُمْ‌ؕ اَنْتُمْ قَدَّمْتُمُوْهُ لَنَا‌ۚ فَبِئْسَ الْقَرَارُ‏(60)\nQAALOO BAL ANTUM LAA MARHABAN BEKUM ANTUM QADDAMTUMOOHU LANAA FA MASALUL AL-QARAARU.\nThey shall say: “Nay! ye too! there shall be no welcome for you; Indeed ye did prepare this for us; and wretched is the abode!\nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا مَنْ قَدَّمَ لَنَا هٰذَا فَزِدْهُ عَذَابًا ضِعْفًا فِى النَّارِ‏(61)\nQAALOO RABBANAA MAN QADDAMA LANAA HAAZAA FAZEDHU A’ZAABAN ZEA’FAN FIL NAAR.\nThey shall say: “O’ our Lord! Whoever hath brought this for us, increase Thou a twofold torment in the fire.\nوَقَالُوْا مَا لَنَا لَا نَرٰى رِجَالًا كُنَّا نَعُدُّهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَشْرَارِؕ‏(62)\nWA QAALOO MAA LANAA LAA NARAA REJAALAN KUNNAA NAU’UDDUHUM MENAL AL-AASHRAARE.\nAnd they shall say: “What hath happened unto us that we see not the men whom we counted among the wicked ones?\nاَ تَّخَذْنٰهُمْ سِخْرِيًّا اَمْ زَاغَتْ عَنْهُمُ الْاَبْصَارُ‏(63)\nA’ZAABAN TTAKHAZNAAHUM SEKHREEA AM ZAAGHAT A’NHOMUL IZ ZAAGHATIL.\nWhat! was it that we (wrongly) took them to scorn, or have our eyes turned from them?\nاِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ لَحَقّ ٌ تَخَاصُمُ اَهْلِ النَّارِ‏(64)\nINNAL ZAA LEKA LAHAQQ TAKHAASUMU AHLIL NAAR.\nVerily, this is truth - the wrangling of one with another of the inmates of the fire.\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا مُنْذِرٌ ‌‌ۖ  وَّمَا مِنْ اِلٰهٍ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ‌ ۚ‏(65)\nQUL INNAMAA ANAA MUNZERUN WA MAA MIN ELAAHIN ILLAA LAAHO AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “I am only a warner and there is no god but God the One, The Almighty!\nرَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا الْعَزِيْزُ الْغَفَّارُ‏(66)\nRABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA A’ZEEZUL AL-GHAFFAARU.\nLord of the heavens and the earth, and what is between them two, the Almighty, the Most Forgiving.\nقُلْ هُوَ نَبَؤٌا عَظِيْمٌۙ‏(67)\nQUL HOWA NABAUNA A’ZEEM.\nSay thou: “It is a message of (great) importance,\nاَنْتُمْ عَنْهُ مُعْرِضُوْنَ‏(68)\nANTUM A’NHO MUA’REZOONA.\n(And) ye are turning away from it.\nمَا كَانَ لِىَ مِنْ عِلْمٍۢ بِالْمَلَاِ الْاَعْلٰٓى اِذْ يَخْتَصِمُوْنَ‏(69)\nMAA KAANA LEYA MIN I’LMIN BE-MALA-E AL-AAA’LAAA IZ YAKHTASEMOON.\nI had no knowledge of the exalted chiefs when they disputed!\nاِنْ يُّوْحٰۤى اِلَىَّ اِلَّاۤ اَنَّمَاۤ اَنَا۟ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(70)\nIN YYOOHAA ELAYYA ILLAA ANNAMAA ANAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nIt is revealed unto me save that I am an open Warner.\nاِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اِنِّىْ خَالِقٌ ۢ بَشَرًا مِّنْ طِيْنٍ‏(71)\nIZ QAALA RABBOKA LIL-MALAAA-EKATE INNEE KHAALEQUN BASHARAN MIN TEENIN.\nRemember when thy Lord said unto the angels: “Verily I am about to create man from clay,\nفَاِذَا سَوَّيْتُهٗ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِىْ فَقَعُوْا لَهٗ سٰجِدِيْنَ‏(72)\nFA-EZAA SAWYTUH WANAFAKHTU FEEHE MIN RROOHEAA FAQAU’OOA LAHU SAAJEDEENA.\nAnd when I have completed and have breathed into him of My spirit, then fall ye prostrating in obeisance unto him.\nفَسَجَدَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ كُلُّهُمْ اَجْمَعُوْنَۙ‏(73)\nFASAJADA TAHMELOHUL KULLUHUM AAJMAU’OONA.\nAnd did fall prostrating in obeisance the angels all together,\nاِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اِسْتَكْبَرَ وَكَانَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(74)\nILLAA IBLEES AESTAKBARA KAANAL MENAL KAAFEREEN.\nSave Iblis; he was proud and was of the disbelievers.\nقَالَ يٰۤاِبْلِيْسُ مَا مَنَعَكَ اَنْ تَسْجُدَ لِمَا خَلَقْتُ بِيَدَىَّ‌ ؕ اَسْتَكْبَرْتَ اَمْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْعَالِيْنَ‏(75)\nQAALA YAABLEESU MAA MANAA’AKA AN TASJUDA LEMAKH KHALAQTU BEEDAA AASTAKBARTA AM KUNTA MENAL AL-A’AALEENA.\nSaid (God): “O’ Iblis! what prevented thee that thou shouldst not prostrate in obeisance unto him whom I created with My two hands? Art thou proud or art thou of the exalted ones?\nقَالَ اَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْهُ‌ ؕ خَلَقْتَنِىْ مِنْ نَّارٍ وَّخَلَقْتَهٗ مِنْ طِيْنٍ‏(76)\nQAALA ANAA KHAYRUL MINHO KHALAQTANEAA MIN NAAR WWAKHALAQTAH MIN TEENIN.\nSaid he: “I am better than he: Thou hast created me of fire and Thou didst create him from clay.\nقَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَاِنَّكَ رَجِيْمٌ  ۖ‌ ۚ‏(77)\nQAALA FAKHRUJ MINHAA FA-INNAKA RAJEEMUN.\nSaid (God): “Begone thou out of it, for verily thou art the outcast one!\nوَّاِنَّ عَلَيْكَ لَعْنَتِىْۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ‏(78)\nWWAANNA A’LAYKA LAA’NATEAA ELAA YAWMIL DEENE.\nAnd verily on thee shall be My curse to the Day of Judgment.\nقَالَ رَبِّ فَاَنْظِرْنِىْۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(79)\nQAALA RABBE FAANZERNEAA ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\nHe said: “O’ my Lord! then Respite me to the Day when they (Adam and his posterity) will be raised,\nقَالَ فَاِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِيْنَۙ‏(80)\nQAALA FA-INNAKA MENAL AL-MUNZAREENA.\nSaid (God): “Verily then thou art of the respited ones,\nاِلٰى يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُوْمِ‏(81)\nELAA YAWMIL AL-WAQTE AL-MAA’LOOME.\nTill the day of the time made known!\nقَالَ فَبِعِزَّتِكَ لَاُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(82)\nQAALA FABEE’EZZATEKA LAAGHWEENNAHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nSaid he: “Then by Thy Might, I will certainly beguile them all,\nاِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(83)\nILLAA E’EBAADAKA MENHUMU AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nSave Thy servants from among them the freed ones,\nقَالَ فَالْحَقُّ  وَالْحَقَّ اَ قُوْلُ‌ ۚ‏(84)\nQAALA FA HAQQO WA HAQQA A’ZAABAN QOOLU.\nHe said: “Then it is the truth - and the truth do I speak,\nلَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنْكَ وَمِمَّنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(85)\nLAAMLAANNA JAHANNAMA MENKA WA MIMMAN TABEA’AKA MINHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nCertainly, will I fill hell with thee and with those who follow thee, all (together)\nقُلْ مَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ وَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُتَكَلِّفِيْنَ‏(86)\nQUL MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN WA MAA ANAA MENAL AL-MUTAKALLEFEENA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I ask ye not for any recompense for it; nor am I of the imposters\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(87)\nIN HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUNW LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nIt is naught but a Reminder unto the worlds\nوَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ نَبَاَهٗ بَعْدَ حِيْنِ‏(88)\nWALATAA’LAMUNNA NABAAH BA’DA HEENE.\nAnd certainly ye will come to know about it after a time.",
  "merits": "Surah Saad\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 88 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is written that the reward for reciting this Surah is equal to the weight of the mountain of Prophet Dawood (a.s.). Allah (s.w.t.) inspires the reciter of this Surah to avoid every type of sin – big or small.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the reward for reciting Surah Saad is compared to the reward given to the Holy Prophets and the one who often recites this Surah will be taken to Jannah along with his family and loved ones; to such an extent that even those servants of his whom he loves will be with him in Jannah.\nIf this Surah is placed under the tyrant ruler, his reign will not last for more than three days before people will see his true nature and will start hating him. This will eventually lead to his downfall."
